allot."]}, "overview": "Maine's 2nd District is an open seat after Jared Golden's retirement, and it sits in Republican-leaning territory. Former Governor Paul LePage brings strong name recognition and a large fundraising lead over Democrat Matt Dunlap, a former secretary of state. Most expert raters call the race a Republican-leaning flip, though a few call it a tossup or even Lean D, and prediction markets give LePage roughly a two-thirds chance.\n\nPolling is thin but recent surveys put Dunlap slightly ahead, including an academic poll showing a six-point lead. The race has featured active debates over property taxes, health care, and immigration. With the fundamentals favoring Republicans and polls favoring Democrats by a hair, this sits as a genuine tossup with a slight Republican tilt.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4239, "margin": -1.15}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.38, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3812, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.377, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3179, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4062, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4214, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.437, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4556, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4353, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4338, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4042, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.4713, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3776, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.3456, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.3722, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.4333, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.4085, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.406, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.3777, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.4678, "margin